{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_019mVvexg8yEDbqU9pAZqtW9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's what was completed this run:\n\n**Task completed:** `answers/08-003-detect-policy-violations-offensive-content.md`\n\n**Key content written:**\n- **Framing:** Probes whether you can translate \"prevent bad outputs\" into a concrete, measurable detection pipeline — distinguishing provider filters, custom classifiers, and rules layers.\n- **Answer:** Two-boundary, three-tier detection stack:\n  1. *Input (synchronous):* Fast regex/blocklist (PII patterns, known terms) → **Llama Guard 3** for Tier-1 harms (CSAM, violence, self-harm) in <60ms\n  2. *Output:* Fine-tuned **DistilBERT/DeBERTa** for company-specific Tier-2 policy violations — synchronous for high-liability domains (healthcare, finance), async Kafka pipeline for medium-risk apps\n  3. *Async audit:* Kafka stream → human review queue → monthly classifier retraining loop\n- **Calibration detail:** PR curves (not ROC) per harm category — Tier-1 needs recall >99%, Tier-2 needs FP <0.5%\n- **Concrete example:** E-commerce bot at 1.2M queries/day — Tier-1 recall 99.3%, Tier-2 FP 0.4%, over-refusal 0.38%\n\n**Remaining in Next:** Q4 (prompt injection/jailbreaking), Q5–Q10, validate"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":423,"cache_read_input_tokens":81788,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":423,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa2a920e-71cb-4b8e-87cd-ff0ac5fb25f7","uuid":"2c288460-3a64-4aa0-8601-314989ca8b44"}
